WEBVTT

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.660
Damn, I'm frozen to the bone.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.530
Are we getting close to Japanese waters?

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.220
Yeah, won't be long now.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.540
We finally made it home...

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:27.980
Where's Souya?

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:29.040
I don't know.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.740
He was right over there 
snoring away a moment ago.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.570
<b>Undisclosed Line</b>

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:53.570
This is...

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:12.170
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:12.170
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:27.190
BURANKI

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:30.860
BURANKI

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:34.650
BURANKI

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.550
Kazuki

00:01:53.750 --> 00:01:54.550
Kaoruko

00:02:23.370 --> 00:02:25.450
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.450
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.000
<b><i>BUBUKI/BURANKI</i></b>

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:27.000
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.040
<b>Warning: Approaching Craft</b>

00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:31.920
A flying craft approaching at high speed...

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:36.920
These heart waveforms... 
The Buranki Mega-lala?

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.440
Epizo...

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.820
Azuma, you are a good guy.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:02.530
If Buranki hadn't been involved,

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:05.330
I'm sure we could've been 
the best of friends.

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:08.330
But unfortunately, I have to defeat you!

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:12.790
For the sake of the reason 
I found for fighting...

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:15.740
For the one who's most important to me!

00:03:29.810 --> 00:03:31.880
Madame Kazuki...

00:03:31.880 --> 00:03:35.650
I had hoped to one day have 
a long talk with you.

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:39.830
I must express my gratitude at 
this opportunity to meet the

00:03:39.830 --> 00:03:42.390
woman of legend in person...

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:45.120
For the fall of the Celestial Rock Cave.

00:03:45.650 --> 00:03:49.040
Don't you mean "for making it fall"?

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:59.250
Human life lasts but a short 
hundred years at best.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:03.510
How, with such limits, do they manage 
to achieve such growth and prosperity?

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.550
Why do you think that is?

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:08.470
Because we've carried on what was left to us

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.310
by those who came before, perhaps?

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:18.810
Precisely.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.330
The beings known as humans 
are truly remarkable.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.570
They weave their culture and history 
through the intermingling of bloodlines.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:32.080
That is the special privilege of humans, 
the beings made in the likeness of God.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.210
You seem to believe that humans 
are at the center of this world.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.750
Well, naturally.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.960
That humans are the most valuable of all?

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:42.340
Of course.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.720
Then why do you think it is

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:51.690
that this world is too vast for any 
human to walk across in a lifetime?

00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.350
Well, now, I've never thought about that.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:04:59.700
Have you ever thought about the significance

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:04.540
of the fact that this endlessly 
vast world sustains creatures

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.360
too small for our eyes to see?

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.780
What are you trying to say?

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:14.580
The world simply allows us 
humans to live upon it.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.020
You're wrong.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:21.320
That is no more than a nihilistic notion 
meant to belittle the human race.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:23.340
It's foolishness.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:29.140
Your head is truly filled with 
love for the human race.

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.350
So much so that you would crush this world.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:51.610
Laetitia's gonna die at this rate!

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:54.120
But with the help of Buranki...

00:05:56.240 --> 00:06:00.040
Laetitia can keep flying forever!

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:07.660
Epizo, I understand your 
reason for fighting now.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.300
But I'll fight, too!

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.240
So I can crush the ambitions of Guy,

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.210
the one who brought down
Treasure Island and deceived Kaoruko!

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:20.900
I got it, Azuma!

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:25.910
This means whichever one of 
us wins is right, doesn't it?

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:30.640
Then instead of grumbling, let's settle 
this once and for all with our fists!

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.530
Yeah, all right.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:47.340
I have no interest in
why the Buranki crossed the

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.680
sea of stars to reach Earth.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.470
But what I hate is the fact

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:56.650
that they tainted the human race!

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:03.610
The countless Buranki that fell 
to Earth and into ruin...

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:09.430
Their disgraced bodies broke apart into 
shards and dissolved in the seas,

00:07:09.430 --> 00:07:11.130
then found their way up the food chain

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:14.710
and into the bodies of humans,
accumulating there.

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:19.410
Eventually Bubuki users, humans with 
Rinzu in their bodies, came to exist.

00:07:19.950 --> 00:07:23.460
They are the ones Bubuki 
choose as their masters,

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:27.530
the humans who carry on the 
blood that the Buranki tainted.

00:07:28.690 --> 00:07:30.970
I cannot forgive that!

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.920
Why can't you?

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.760
Why? I should be asking you...

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:39.650
Why are you not angry,

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:43.300
when the blood of our noble 
human race has been tainted?

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:48.780
I will purify everything.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:51.720
I'll destroy the Bubuki and Buranki

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:55.100
and kill every last Bubuki user.

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:58.870
How ironic it is that I must use Deus Magna,

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.870
the god of the Buranki, 
to achieve that purpose.

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:06.000
It's not possible to resurrect 
the Buranki's progenitor!

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:10.310
I'm sure you intend to stop me 
from resurrecting Deus Magna,

00:08:10.310 --> 00:08:14.550
but do you honestly think I'll 
just let you leave here quietly?

00:08:29.380 --> 00:08:30.510
A-chan!

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:32.200
You okay, Azuma?!

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:34.610
I can't...

00:08:34.890 --> 00:08:35.760
Huh?

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.990
Azuma, why are you laughing?

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:43.080
I was just wondering why 
Oubu and I share pain.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.460
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.880
If I'm hurting this much,

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.440
I hope Oubu isn't feeling the same pain.

00:08:50.990 --> 00:08:52.440
A-chan...

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:55.770
I don't know how you can be so 
flippant at a time like this.

00:08:55.770 --> 00:08:58.130
Azuma, the king of flippancy.

00:08:58.130 --> 00:08:59.690
King Flip.

00:09:02.110 --> 00:09:04.520
Hey, Epizo! How long are 
you gonna lie there?

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.200
Get a grip!

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.030
Did he get hit in a bad spot?

00:09:08.030 --> 00:09:10.020
He must have, he must have!

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:11.990
It's not that.

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:15.520
After hitting each other 
as hard as we could,

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:19.160
my head feels totally empty and clear now!

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:23.160
That's the great thing about you, Epizo.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:26.000
That empty head of yours.

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.510
No doubt about that.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:33.880
Laetitia!

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:36.840
Epizo!

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:43.580
Laetitia! You got Epimew back!

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:47.140
Now break its heart and 
go into Epimew's brain!

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:51.150
Then you'll have a body 
that can move freely!

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:55.110
Break the heart and go into Epimew's brain?

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.160
Epizo, what are you saying?!

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.230
She can't! If she does that...

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.830
Thank you, Azuma! I get it now!

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:07.530
I was able to figure it out 
thanks to my empty head.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.140
Everything Guy says is a lie!

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:11.630
He's trying to trick me!

00:10:12.140 --> 00:10:16.880
So he must have had some reason 
for returning Epimew to Laetitia.

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:18.200
Epizo...

00:10:18.980 --> 00:10:22.260
Laetitia! Get out of Epimew, quick!

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:23.950
Epizo...

00:10:24.430 --> 00:10:26.430
I don't understand, but okay!

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:32.400
Everyone... what's wrong?

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:38.760
Just like the little rats from Russia,

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:41.820
they were brainwashed long ago.

00:10:43.250 --> 00:10:44.950
Moses...

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.340
It looks like you realized it a bit late,

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.760
Epizo.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:08.270
Now, pseudo-humans with Buranki 
mixed into your blood...

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:12.740
It's only fitting that you non-humans 
should kill each other.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.990
<b>Episode 21
Swan Song</b>

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.990
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI
The Gentle Giants
 of the Galaxy</i></b>

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:22.490
<b><i>BUBUKI BURANKI</i></b>

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.490
<b>The Gentle Giants of the Galaxy</b>

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.950
Azuma, this looks bad!

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:34.710
This is... the inside of a Buranki's head?

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.130
Something's different from before.

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.860
Be careful, Epizo!

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:43.930
R-Right.

00:12:07.640 --> 00:12:10.200
Azuma! I want to save Laetitia!

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.870
Help me!

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:12.400
Right!

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.720
But A-chan, we can't get close this way!

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:16.540
Leave it to me.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:18.880
It's all-or-nothing now!

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.380
Tsurarai!

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:31.730
Laetitia!

00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.110
Now, Azuma!

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:45.500
Thanks, Mega-lala.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:53.830
Laetitia! Laetitia!

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:56.130
Epizo...

00:13:25.340 --> 00:13:26.740
Is this...

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:28.740
the world of the Buranki?

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:08.550
No!

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:19.630
Oh, my God!

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:22.720
What are you doing, Farrah?!

00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:23.680
Epizo!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:27.010
Epizo, thank goodness!

00:14:27.730 --> 00:14:32.720
You wouldn't wake up, so I thought 
maybe if I gave you a little shock...

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:35.380
Farrah...

00:14:36.190 --> 00:14:38.690
What the heck happened to me?

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:43.330
Epizo, the moment you dove into its head,

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:46.690
the Buranki Epimew immediately 
ceased functioning.

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:58.820
And then you were ejected 
from within Epimew's head.

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:06.640
Where's Laetitia?!

00:15:11.510 --> 00:15:12.670
Laetitia!

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:15.420
Epizo...

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:39.820
I suppose Laetitia's body 
was unable to withstand

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:42.960
the immense burden of serving 
as a Buranki's brain.

00:15:43.710 --> 00:15:46.500
How can you say that?! You're not human!

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.010
That is exactly what I should say to you,

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:54.440
Kazuki Migiwa, the witch 
spellbound by Buranki.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:55.510
I will also say this:

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.890
Laetitia's death was not in vain.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:00.910
It was a necessary sacrifice

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:04.270
toward acquiring a god 
visible to human eyes.

00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.030
I believe I told you that I won't 
allow you to leave quietly.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:19.860
That's...

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:21.600
The Buranki Zampaza!

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:30.570
Thank you, Souya-kun.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:35.180
Migiwa-san, I've got nothing 
but hard feelings toward you,

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:38.930
but I also realize this is 
not the time for all that.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:41.480
<i>Reoko...</i>

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.190
<b>Undisclosed Line</b>

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.190
<i>Please lend me your help.</i>

00:16:46.390 --> 00:16:48.350
I know this is cowardly,

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:52.560
but I have no other way to 
get to Treasure Island now.

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.490
So I truly thank you.

00:16:56.460 --> 00:16:58.850
I'm sorry to keep asking for help.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:02.960
Please continue from here to the 
waters where Treasure Island fell.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:06.870
We're gonna have to speed up a bit, then!

00:17:15.020 --> 00:17:16.760
I feel bad for them,

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.760
but we need to get moving.

00:17:20.200 --> 00:17:21.280
Azuma...

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:22.880
Azuma-kun.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:25.690
In order to crush Guy's ambition,

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.770
we must destroy Treasure Island.

00:17:27.770 --> 00:17:28.400
What?!

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.690
Destroy... Destroy it?!

00:17:30.690 --> 00:17:34.270
But Treasure Island is still intact 
at the bottom of the sea, right?

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:36.030
So why...

00:17:38.150 --> 00:17:38.820
Right.

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.210
To keep it from being 
used for Guy's purposes,

00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:45.210
it's our only choice.

00:17:45.210 --> 00:17:46.370
But...

00:17:50.320 --> 00:17:51.590
Kaoruko...

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.650
It's really true.

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:11.620
Treasure Island sank in 
its original condition.

00:18:12.140 --> 00:18:17.710
So this Rinzu barrier kept protecting it,
even after it hit the water.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:20.450
And if we don't break through that,

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:23.500
we can't destroy Treasure Island, right?

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.960
You are the daughter of Migiwa?

00:18:33.010 --> 00:18:34.530
Banryuu Reoko...

00:18:35.130 --> 00:18:37.400
Don't call me that.

00:18:37.400 --> 00:18:40.260
I've got a perfectly good name,
and it's Kaoruko!

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:45.270
I see... Your name is Kaoruko, then?

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:48.020
Huh? What about it?

00:18:48.020 --> 00:18:52.270
Thinking you need to introduce yourself 
properly to your archenemy's daughter?

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:54.820
Wh-What? I was right?

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:59.910
Kaoruko, I have something to tell you.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:01.310
Huh?

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:14.290
Azuma!

00:19:14.780 --> 00:19:16.180
Don't do that.

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.960
She's right, A-chan!

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:22.180
If you go into Oubu's head again,
you'll end up like her!

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:25.190
But there's no other way.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:26.890
What else can we do?

00:19:36.670 --> 00:19:37.820
Mom?!

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.830
Damn it!

00:19:48.430 --> 00:19:52.330
That was not cool, Migiwa-san!

00:19:53.410 --> 00:19:55.840
I will sink Treasure Island.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:19:57.540
How?

00:19:57.540 --> 00:20:00.360
I'll make a hole in the 
Rinzu that protects it,

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:04.370
turn it into energy, and make 
it destroy Treasure Island.

00:20:04.370 --> 00:20:05.850
If that's an option, then...

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:07.350
We'll do it with Oubu!

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:09.430
You kids can't do it.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:13.150
But if you do that,
you'll never make it back!

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.930
I'll be fine.

00:20:14.930 --> 00:20:17.150
Don't underestimate the power of a witch.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:20.550
What are you talking about, Mom?!

00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:26.120
Maybe this was necessary all along 
in order to keep Treasure Island

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.000
and the Buranki from being used by humans.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:31.610
But...

00:20:33.520 --> 00:20:34.910
I wish...

00:20:36.840 --> 00:20:39.990
our whole family could have stayed there,

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:42.770
living our lives as we 
protected the Buranki.

00:20:51.860 --> 00:20:54.440
I'm not letting you go this time!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.150
Damn!

00:21:41.150 --> 00:21:43.880
The island's not even scratched!

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:46.700
Is Migiwa's effort gonna go to waste?

00:21:50.630 --> 00:21:52.550
Kazuki Migiwa...

00:21:52.550 --> 00:21:54.960
The witch's last stand

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:59.460
did nothing but accelerate 
the awakening of the comet.
